codex
The first implementation is correct, but its mutable `seen` heap object would make the invariant carry an avoidable heap history. I’m making a semantics-supported refinement: scan each integer and use `list.count` to test whether its inverse occurs, requiring two zeros in the zero case. This preserves the exact contract and yields a direct “some element has a distinct inverse partner” summary while keeping the proof inside fixed semantics.
